w: Com- fort, com- fort ye my peo- ple, Speak ye peace, thus saith our God;
w: Yea, her sins our God will par- don, Blot- ting out each dark mis- deed;
w: For the her- ald's voice is cry- ing In the des- ert far and near,
w: Make ye straight what long was crook- ed, Make the rough- er pla- ces plain:
F2 G A2 G | F E D2 C2 | F2 G A2 B | A2 G2 F2 |
w: Com- fort those who sit in dark- ness, Mourn- ing 'neath their sor- rows' load;
w: All that well de- served His an- ger He no more will see or heed.
w: Bid- ding all men to re- pent- ance, Since the king- dom now is here.
w: Let your hearts be true and hum- ble, As be- fits His ho- ly reign.
A2 A c2 B | [M:2/2] A G A2 | [M:3/2] c2 c d2 c | [M:2/2] B A G2 |
w: Speak ye to Je- ru- sa- lem Of the peace that waits for them;
w: She hath suf- fered man- y~a day, Now her griefs have passed a- way;
w: Oh, that warn- ing cry o- bey! Now pre- pare for God a way!
w: For the glo- ry of the Lord Now o'er earth is shed a- broad;
[M:3/2] A2 c B2 A | F G A2 F2 | A2 A B2 A | G F E2 F2 |]
w: Tell her that her sins I cov- er, And her war- fare now is o- ver.
w: God will change her pin- ing sad- ness In- to ev- er- spring- ing glad- ness.
w: Let the val- leys rise to meet Him, And the hills bow down to greet Him.
w: And all flesh shall see the to- ken That His word is nev- er bro- ken.
